join Zanele (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Zanele: He goes on Thursday. There is nothing that needs doing, which is the difficulty.
- Nothing?
	Hope: Nothing?
	Zanele: He has packed. Gogo has fed him. Naledi has given him a blanket he did not ask for and will not be able to carry.
	Zanele: So there is nothing to arrange, and a week to get through, and I find I would rather be arranging something.
